/// `termination-certificates`: Replayable termination certificates.
/// Implemented: one termination evidence form, a path order's derivation over the precedence as data, replayed by the kernel for an operation's and a theory's rules and read by the front end and the cell layer.
/// Not implemented: a size measure for a fixpoint; #392 owes it.
// A rule written as an equation, `<=>`: one term spelled two ways, with the
// left side the one a reader would rewrite to. The order of terms chooses the
// direction, so `x <=> S(P(x))` still runs `S(P(x))` to `x` (Huet, _Confluent
// reductions_, doi:10.1145/322217.322230). The integers are named apart from
// the base's, whose rules are written the other way round.

/// The integers with their first rule written smaller side first.
@[ normalizes("S(P(Z)) ~> Z") ]
data IntEq : Type {
  Z : IntEq;
  S : (x : IntEq) --> IntEq;
  P : (x : IntEq) --> IntEq;
  rule x <=> S(P(x));
  rule P(S(x)) <=> x;
}
